==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Warlock and Pierre were a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Merchant + Courier (Removed Combo)|Merchant + Courier]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], Mad Doctor Klay was one of the few [[:Category:Cats with Ultra Talents|Cats with Ultra Talents]] to lack a second [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slot.
*Warlock and Pierre and [[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Detective Vigler]] are the only [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] who increase their stats in True Form.
*Mad Doctor Klay currently has the highest base attack power of all Cat Units, with 163,455 at level 30.
*Mad Doctor Klay and [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]] are the only units that can hurt one trait.
*Mad Doctor Klay likely takes inspiration from [[wikipedia:Mary Shelley|Mary Shelley's]] ''[[wikipedia:Frankenstein|Frankenstein]]'', as referenced to by the occult anatomy and soul transplant mentions in Mad Doctor Klay's description.
*The tagline for Dark Merchant Babil on the Dark Heroes English poster, reading "Collecting wicked souls is their business... and business is GOOD!", may be a reference to the 1985 thrash metal album [[wikipedia:Killing Is My Business... and Business Is Good!|Killing Is My Business... and Business is Good!]].
*Dark Merchant Babil was the first Uber Rare to have the [[Money Up]] ability.
*This is currently the only Cat Unit to have the [[Base Destroyer]] ability.
**However, [[Honda Tadakatsu (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Honda Tadakatsu]] also had the ability before the PC version was removed.

